<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Burma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> is the inland, northern part of Myanmar around the middle Irrawaddy, including the dry zone where Pagan, Ava and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a> stood. It was the heartland of most Burmese kingdoms, in contrast to the Mon country of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-burmese-war">Third Anglo-Burmese War</a> in 1885, together with the Shan states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-burma.jpg" alt="Upper Burma" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Al Bagania · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Two_Geopolitical_Regions_of_Myanmar.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
